# Placeholder so `go build` works without a UI build.
#
# go:embed fails when its target directory is absent, and the real files only exist after the
# frontend build (see the Dockerfile). Without this file a plain `go build ./...` — which the unit
# CI job runs on every push — would fail on a clean checkout, for a reason unrelated to Go.
#
# The Docker build overwrites this directory (`COPY --from=ui /ui/dist`), so a released image holds
# the real bundle. A local `go run` serves only this file, which is the honest behaviour: no UI was
# built.
